   "text": {
    "L1": "When we say a fraction of another fraction, of means multiply.",
    "L2": "For example, 3/5 of 2/3 is 3/5 times 2/3.",
    "L3": "An area model shows 2/3 shaded, then 3/5 of that shading.",
    "L4": "Six of fifteen small parts are shaded twice, so the product is 6/15.",
    "L5": "Multiply numerators and denominators: 3 times 2 is 6, and 5 times 3 is 15.",
    "L6": "Simplify 6/15 by dividing by 3. The answer is 2/5 of the cake.",
    "L7": "Multiplication does not always make a number bigger. Ten times one half is five, which is smaller than ten.",
    "L8": "Now choose the product for 3/5 of 2/3."
   },
